vorbis_setup.bin: the Vorbis setup headers (type 5 packets) that FMOD's encoder writes, keyed by the
CRC32 that FSB5 stores in a sample's Vorbis chunk (FSB5 strips the three Vorbis headers from every
stream).

Source: python-fsb5, fsb5/vorbis_headers.py, https://github.com/HearthSim/python-fsb5 (the file is a
`lookup = {crc32: setup_packet}` table of 161 entries).  Only the 23 entries that the ArcheAge 1.2
banks use are kept here; crates/aa-audio/tools/make_setup_table.py rebuilds the file (all entries or a
chosen list of CRCs) from that source.

